  "answer": "**Final status: passed.** The second verification run (`20261021T142229Z-3a6d2d`) passed build, unit and component. The fix took one round.\n\n**What failed:** The first run (`20261021T142131Z-e141f1`) failed at the unit stage, so the component stage never ran. The build was fine. Two tests failed on both net9.0 and net10.0:\n1. `DeltaFormatterTests.Format_FieldInActualNotInExpected_ShowsAbsentSentinel`\n2. `HttpReadinessProbeTests.TryProbe_ServerReturns500_ReturnsFalse`\n\n**Root cause:**\n1. **A real bug in the library.** In `src/ConfIT/Matching/DeltaFormatter.cs:69`, when a field is in the actual response but not the expected one, the diff output printed the placeholder `<not present>`. The test expects `<absent>`.\n2. **A flaky test, not a code bug.** This one threw `HttpListenerException: Address already in use` while closing its listener (`test/ConfIT.UnitTest/Server/Http/AppLauncherTests.cs:183`). It doesn't touch the library code. The fixer thinks it's a port clash: the test stops the listener and then closes it again, possibly while other tests run in parallel or with a port that was already taken. It passed on the second run without changes.\n\n**What was changed:** One line in `src/ConfIT/Matching/DeltaFormatter.cs:69` now prints `<absent>` instead of `<not present>`. Nothing else was edited, and nothing was committed.\n\n**Follow-up:** The readiness-probe test passed this time, but nothing about it changed, so it may fail again. If it does, the fixer suggests removing its extra `listener.Stop()` call or making port allocation more robust.",
